d99067b8f40f1a1","event_uuid":"150d3c74-e1bb-4ba3-8074-b3c1db114f0d","position":{"commit_sha":"3e6f28309728e78b536f9190a14c8dc287cb7e3b","position":"1786558718379702001-150d3c74-e1bb-4ba3-8074-b3c1db114f0d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2bdfcbb434741c676648bd6051a7ecf684a724c59fbfb62fbc35bff0731318fd","event_uuid":"f387c7cf-a896-452a-bfb1-2644afae2acd","position":{"commit_sha":"e47092901e0b5e8ea76d90fd9edee6a8fc884027","position":"1786559702593428292-f387c7cf-a896-452a-bfb1-2644afae2acd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[],"created_at":1786529773041626001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"87169e70-2212-435c-8df9-30bf34e4d93c","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"1647-19b3-cbec-4a17"},{"link_uuid":"f387c7cf-a896-452a-bfb1-2644afae2acd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4352-2c05-2fe3-4b77"}],"description":"## Context\n\nChange 78257ce2ff (willing-cellular-carp, Gerrit 1652) fixed ONE site in\ntests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py where a two-clone fixture established its\nshared-base precondition via an unasserted side effect of `_engine_run(repo, \"list\")`. The\nbest-effort `ensure_fresh` read path swallows every failure by design, so under CI load the\nprecondition silently fails and the test dies in setup (flake signature:\n`AssertionError: clones do not share a base`).\n\nThe same `_expire_sync_marker` + `_engine_run(...)` pattern appears at 23 further sites in that\nfile. Each is a candidate instance of the identical flake mechanism.\n\n## Audit result (AC1)\n\nAll 23 `_expire_sync_marker` call sites were enumerated against `ensure_fresh`'s best-effort\ncontract and split into two kinds:\n\n**Kind P — load-bearing fixture PRECONDITION (8 sites).** The sync must land for the test to\nmean anything; a sync that silently does not land produces a misleading or absent failure.\nLines 378, 398, 460, 1236, 1325, 1333, 1476, 1580. In each, one clone is strictly BEHIND the\nother (the peer has just pushed), so a checked fetch + ff-only merge reproduces the intended\nstate deterministically.\n\n**Kind R — the read-side sync IS the behavior under test (15 sites).** Lines 225, 229, 319,\n321, 343, 345, 469, 471, 507, 1085, 1117, 1242, 1339, 1505, 1507. These tests characterize\n\"a clone reconverges through the real production read path\"; the assertion that follows IS the\nconvergence claim. Driving them through raw git would delete the invariant they exist to\nprove, and a failure there is a TRUE signal, not a misleading setup failure. They are therefore\ncorrectly left on `_engine_run(..., \"list\")` — but the reason is currently implicit.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Convert the 8 Kind-P sites to the existing `_sync_from_origin` helper (defined line 1680:\n   checked `git fetch` + checked ff-only `git merge`), deleting the paired\n   `_expire_sync_marker(...)` / `_engine_run(..., \"list\")` lines at 378-379, 398-399, 460-461,\n   1236-1237, 1325-1326, 1333-1334, 1476-1477, 1580-1581. Where a converted site already had a\n   downstream precondition assert, keep it and mark it SETUP so a red there reads as a harness\n   failure rather than an invariant failure.\n2. Move `_sync_from_origin` up to the helper block near `_expire_sync_marker` (line 76) so it\n   is defined before its first use, and extend its docstring with the Kind-P / Kind-R rule so\n   the next author picks correctly.\n3. Give Kind R a single named home: add `_reconverge_by_read_sync(repo, tracker, *, passes)`\n   beside it, encapsulating the repeated expire+`list` idiom, whose docstring records WHY the\n   best-effort path is deliberate here (the read-side reconvergence is the assertion target, so\n   its failure is the finding). Route all 15 Kind-R sites through it; the two-pass sites pass\n   `passes=2`, the single-pass sites `passes=1`. No behavior change at those sites.\n4. Prove AC3: run the file under `REBAR_SYNC_PULL=off` and under default env.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py -q` (default env, baseline is 29 passed).\n- `REBAR_SYNC_PULL=off env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py -q` — the reproduction switch that proved the original flake.\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` and `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 — checked by grep audit: Enumerate every site in tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py that relies on `_engine_run(...)`'s incidental sync to establish a fixture precondition (grep for `_expire_sync_marker` and `_engine_run` pairs; verify against `ensure_fresh`'s best-effort contract).\n- [ ] AC2 — checked by review of each converted site: Convert each such precondition to the deterministic `_sync_from_origin` helper landed in 78257ce2ff (checked fetch + ff-only merge), or record per-site why the incidental sync is genuinely not load-bearing there.\n- [ ] AC3 — proved by `REBAR_SYNC_PULL=off python -m pytest tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py -q`: The file's tests pass with `REBAR_SYNC_PULL=off` for every converted site's setup path (the reproduction switch that proved the original flake), and under default env.\n- [ ] AC4 — proved by `make lint` and `make typecheck`: `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass; no wall-clock assertions introduced.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py","reason":"convert sync-by-side-effect fixture preconditions to the deterministic _sync_from_origin helper"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","4352-2c05-2fe3-4b77"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"c9c964a6-d8fe-4e71-92b4-3fe0244ccd4a","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"49be-be9e-9c83-494c","ticket_type":"task","title":"Audit remaining sync-by-side-effect fixture sites in test_concurrency_regression.py","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["635d2799-6fb1-4d5f-8092-89f67c7abfbe","87169e70-2212-435c-8df9-30bf34e4d93c","c45aba60-589d-4068-91af-b461d9e4d322","36567904-31e8-4574-9f41-430214f34003","b7b34ae4-53bf-4369-ac7b-3ed6e2acdc6f","99d4ff1f-f8e2-40b4-9654-ced861467dfc","c9c964a6-d8fe-4e71-92b4-3fe0244ccd4a","150d3c74-e1bb-4ba3-8074-b3c1db114f0d","f387c7cf-a896-452a-bfb1-2644afae2acd"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786559702593428293,"uuid":"bda1cf55-3f41-49f0-8252-198c343799cb"}